{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"ecce3c3491f78cf9e72cbf57bf35d1f85bff1d454a62078846d56c63abd38edc","packTokens":1322,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":206,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":308,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":702,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"No test may count on those rows, because the app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Do not build screens here; the web app is built in its own repo.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should authentication and authorization be enforced only where contracts/openapi.yaml explicitly requires them, or should additional access rules be added?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Enforce only authentication/authorization requirements explicitly declared by contracts/openapi.yaml; do not add extra role rules.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen for paths or HTTP methods that are not defined in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal 404/405 responses and add no undocumented operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If demo seed data cannot be written to PostgreSQL when Seed:Demo is true, how should startup behave?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup and surface the seed-write error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Should successful API writes remain available after the API process restarts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal PostgreSQL durability so successful writes remain available after an API restart.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement the Feedlot API to conform to every operation, schema, status, and security rule in the OpenAPI contract, expose no undocumented operations, and provide no product-screen routes or rendered screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined authentication, session, dashboard, and filtered lot data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Support procurement imports and allocations with persisted PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen traceability, matching, and conflict results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Support forecast, forecast-setting, metric, insight, planner-action, and weight-history operations with contract-defined calculations, explainable results, validation, and persisted updates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Support inventory reads, writes, movements, projections, and CSV exports using contract-defined values, and persist valid inventory changes in PostgreSQL.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Support ration reads, creation, revision, optimization, and approval with contract-defined data, calculations, and persisted changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Support feed-plan reads, creation, review, and status changes with contract-defined pen-level details, calculated quantities, audit state, and persistence.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Support feeding-event reads, creation, correction, and voiding with contract-defined variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, and updated lot feed totals.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Support operational, feed-to-gain, and profitability reports and exports with contract-defined calculations, summaries, filters, permissions, and artifacts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Support sample-data reads, loads, resets, and replacements with contract-defined status, no duplicate loading, and explicit confirmation for resets or replacements.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Store contract domain data in the configured App PostgreSQL database, preserve successful writes across API restarts, and upgrade the schema without losing existing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, run SeedData.Run at startup to add 3 to 5 believable contract-example-derived rows to each empty application table, leave nonempty tables unchanged, and fail startup with a surfaced error if seeding fails.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, serve collection operations from persisted records, including empty collections when no records exist.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}